# A founding body may carry non-mandatory prose sections beyond the MADR
# mandatory set and '## Rules' — e.g. a "## Deferred bets" section recording
# open research bets alongside the founding decisions. ExtractSections is
# permissive about which headings appear (body.go), so such a section is
# preserved verbatim in the log (constitution/adr/ADR-0001-*.md) but is never
# rendered into constitution/constitution.md — bets are durable, never
# projected (milestone #4, plan-wide decision #20(b)).

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

exec constitution init --founding-file founding.md --target claude

grep 'Deferred bets' constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md
grep 'Transport stays an open research bet until stage-2 lands.' constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md
grep 'Hexagonal core.' constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md

# the bets section is durable in the log but never projected.
! grep 'Deferred bets' constitution/constitution.md
! grep 'Transport stays an open research bet' constitution/constitution.md
grep 'Hexagonal core.' constitution/constitution.md

exec constitution guard
stdout 'clean'

-- founding.md --
## Context and Problem Statement

Established at project bootstrap by `constitution init`.

## Considered Options

- Adopt this founding decision
- Leave the convention implicit

## Decision Outcome

Hexagonal core.

## Rules

### architecture

#### hex-core
Hexagonal core.

## Deferred bets

Transport stays an open research bet until stage-2 lands.
